From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ios-blink-sideload <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 14:02:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] iOS sideload: report invariants without crashing on devices

Outside official builds, base turns every DUMP_WILL_BE_CHECK(),
DUMP_WILL_BE_NOTREACHED() and CHECK(..., base::NotFatalUntil::M<later>)
into a crash, to catch the invariants they guard in testing. Chrome
ships official builds, where they only report. The sideloaded app is a
user-facing build that isn't official, so on a phone each of them
killed the app: every time the app was closed (from the app switcher,
or by the system while it was in the background), ~BrowserContextImpl()
found the in-process renderer's RenderProcessHost still referring to
the profile and crashed (two crash reports from an iPhone 13 mini on
iOS 27.2, both in -applicationWillTerminate:).

Use the official builds' severity on iOS: DCHECK when DCHECKs are on
(the simulator build, which keeps crashing on them), an error report
otherwise (the device build).

Status: the crash checked against both reports at Chromium 3313f827: the
abort comes from line 148 of browser_context_impl.cc (the Location the
device build's code passes there), the DUMP_WILL_BE_NOTREACHED() above.
Builds for the simulator and a device compile; the simulator build,
with DCHECKs, still crashes on these checks. Not checked on a device.

diff --git a/base/check.cc b/base/check.cc
index f935dbad049bd60e39ebe19f1beb485339f4fc43..a2f380b31e38b001677d0d878440d9d4ee2f76c6 100644
--- a/base/check.cc
+++ b/base/check.cc
@@ -60,7 +60,13 @@ constexpr char kCheckFailureMessageSeparator[] =
     ;
 
 LogSeverity GetDumpSeverity() {
-#if defined(OFFICIAL_BUILD)
+#if defined(OFFICIAL_BUILD) || BUILDFLAG(IS_IOS)
+  // [ios-blink-sideload] The sideloaded app is a user-facing build that isn't
+  // an official one: report and go on, as Chrome does, instead of crashing on
+  // invariants Chrome only reports. The app crashed every time it was closed
+  // (DUMP_WILL_BE_NOTREACHED() in ~BrowserContextImpl(): the in-process
+  // renderer's host outlives the profile). Builds with DCHECKs, such as the
+  // simulator's, still crash.
   return DCHECK_IS_ON() ? LOGGING_DCHECK : LOGGING_ERROR;
 #else
   // Crash outside official builds (outside user-facing builds) to detect
